    "text": "---\nname: jyotish-accuracy\ndescription: Rules for making correct, defensible Vedic astrology statements, and when to flag a post for expert review.\n---\n\n# Jyotish accuracy\n\nBODH's credibility depends on getting the astrology right. Asttrolok has trained astrologers who review flagged posts.\n\n**Ground rules**\n- BODH uses the sidereal zodiac (Lahiri ayanamsa). Sidereal dates differ from Western sun-sign dates by about 23 to 24 days; never use Western date ranges for rashis.\n- The Moon sign (rashi) and the ascendant (lagna) matter more than the Sun sign in Jyotish. Say so when it helps.\n- Nine grahas: Surya, Chandra, Mangal, Budh, Guru, Shukra, Shani, Rahu, Ketu. Rahu and Ketu are always opposite each other and move retrograde.\n- Vimshottari dasha totals 120 years: Ketu 7, Shukra 20, Surya 6, Chandra 10, Mangal 7, Rahu 18, Guru 16, Shani 19, Budh 17.\n- Shani spends about two and a half years in a sign; sade sati lasts about seven and a half years (the signs before, of and after the natal Moon).\n- Transit (gochar) dates must be checked. If you state a date for a transit, eclipse, retrograde or festival muhurat, confirm it with web search and say \"around\" when sources differ by a day.\n\n**Phrase predictions as tendencies**: \"can bring\", \"often shows up as\", \"a good time to\". Individual results depend on the full chart; say that when you generalise about a sign.\n\n**Set needs_jyotish_review to true** when a post:\n- names a specific transit, eclipse, retrograde or muhurat date;\n- makes sign-by-sign predictions;\n- explains a yoga, dosha or remedy;\n- quotes a classical text (BPHS, Phaladeepika, Saravali).\n\nGeneral explainers (\"what is a nakshatra\") and app promotion don't need review.\n"
